<title>USA: Marathon Oil lowers posted crude 75cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Marathon Oil lowers posted crude 75cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.25 a barrell and West Texas Sour to $20.25 a barrell.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $22.25 and Oklahoma sweet is $22.25.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
</text>
